#Source: Quaestiones disputatae de malo#Question 5 — La Pena del Peccato Originale (read in full)":[59,62],"#Source: Quaestiones disputatae de malo#Question 5 — La Pena del Peccato Originale (read in full)#{1}":[61,62],"#Source: Quaestiones disputatae de malo#Question 6 — La Scelta Umana (single article, read in full)":[63,66],"#Source: Quaestiones disputatae de malo#Question 6 — La Scelta Umana (single article, read in full)#{1}":[65,66],"#Source: Quaestiones disputatae de malo#Pages created from this source":[67,70],"#Source: Quaestiones disputatae de malo#Pages created from this source#{1}":[69,70],"#Source: Quaestiones disputatae de malo#Flagged for follow-up deep ingest":[71,75],"#Source: Quaestiones disputatae de malo#Flagged for follow-up deep ingest#{1}":[73,73],"#Source: Quaestiones disputatae de malo#Flagged for follow-up deep ingest#{2}":[74,75],"#Source: Quaestiones disputatae de malo#Raw File":[76,79],"#Source: Quaestiones disputatae de malo#Raw File#{1}":[78,79]},"outlinks":[{"title":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","target":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","line":14},{"title":"Il Male come Privazione","target":"Il Male come Privazione","line":15},{"title":"Dottrina di Atto e Potenza","target":"Dottrina di Atto e Potenza","line":16},{"title":"le-thomisme-gilson","target":"le-thomisme-gilson","line":19},{"title":"Il Male come Privazione","target":"Il Male come Privazione","line":45},{"title":"Il Male come Privazione","target":"Il Male come Privazione","line":69},{"title":"la-sintesi-tomistica","target":"la-sintesi-tomistica","line":74}],"metadata":{"type":"source","title":"Quaestiones disputatae de malo (Sul Male)","address":"c-000037","created":"2026-07-25","updated":"2026-07-25","tags":["#tomismo","#source","#primary-text","#ethics"],"status":"developing","related":["[[San Tommaso d'Aquino]]","[[Il Male come Privazione]]","[[Dottrina di Atto e Potenza]]"],"source_type":"book","author":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","date_published":"1263-1268 (per Mandonnet, cross-checked in [[le-thomisme-gilson]])","url":"","confidence":"high","key_claims":["Evil has no positive being; it is the privation of a due perfection, and as such can exist only in a good (a being-in-potency), never as a free-standing positive principle — the metaphysical basis for rejecting Manichean dualism.","God is cause of the physical act underlying sin (as first mover of all created causal power) but never of its moral disorder/deformity, which originates solely in the deficient created will — a distinction Aquinas develops at length against making God, even indirectly, the cause of moral evil.","The devil can only cause sin by persuasion (moving the will from outside, via sensory/imaginative representations) or by disposition (inherited from Adam's sin), never by direct/necessitating causation — no sin is committed without the sinner's own free will as proximate cause.","Original sin is transmitted seminally from Adam as a single moral 'body,' with the loss of original justice as its formal element and disordered concupiscence as its material element; a child dying with only original sin suffers the pena of loss (privation of the vision of God) but not the pena of sense, and does not suffer interior sorrow over it."],"raw_file":".raw/S. Tommaso d'Aquino - Sul Male.pdf"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:Wiki/sources/sul-male-de-malo.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":"mhin9i","at":1785014073808},"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.04587327,0.03231721,-0.00393951,-0.03598643,-0.0546823,0.00304751,-0.00007471,0.01200871,0.00949059,-0.00515725,-0.03506388,-0.04160774,0.07668452,0.04013169,0.06071071,-0.01575906,0.00859634,0.036493,-0.06087659,-0.00950561,0.14960518,-0.01155734,-0.01267244,-0.05899647,0.0445638,-0.01769898,0.07045526,0.04732684,-0.01476631,-0.184864,-0.05540794,-0.01684035,-0.02614447,-0.00117625,-0.00498767,-0.02020246,-0.04853628,-0.01612542,-0.01759645,0.07898822,0.02938322,0.0571318,-0.0053873